# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Real credentials — only .env.example (placeholders) belongs in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?

# Affinity writes a <file>~lock~ sidecar next to any document it has open and
# deletes it on close. Never worth committing — and it reappears every time the
# store banner source is edited.
*~lock~

# Affinity documents. Editable artwork sources, ~19MB each and rewritten whole
# on every save, so each revision adds that much to history permanently. They
# live in ignore/artwork/ instead. Nothing builds from them: Vite only bundles
# assets that source code imports, so these never reached dist, the Capacitor
# assets or the AAB even while one was tracked. The exported .jpg/.png that the
# store listing and the app actually use stay in src/assets.
*.af

# Local scratch — anything under a directory named "ignore"
ignore/
